---
title: Thai yellow curry with chicken and potatoes
servings: 4
tags: [chicken, gluten-free, make-ahead]
cuisine: thai
time: 1 hour 20 minutes
source: Authentic Thai Yellow Curry with Chicken and Potatoes by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/yellow-curry-chicken
---

Skim the thick cream off the @coconut milk{800%ml} into a #medium pot{}. Add the @yellow curry paste{4%oz}, set over medium heat, and fry, stirring, until very thick and the oil separates.

Add the rest of the coconut milk, the @chicken thighs{2%lb}, @fish sauce{1%tbsp}, @palm sugar{1 1/2%tbsp}, @tamarind paste{1%tbsp} and just enough @water{1%cup} to cover. Simmer gently ~{30%minutes}.

Meanwhile nick the @cherry tomatoes{1%cup} with a knife tip so they do not burst.

Add the @waxy potatoes{1%lb}(cut in 1-inch chunks), @carrots{2}(cut on the diagonal into chunks) and @onion{1/2}(cut in 1 cm strips). Simmer ~{15%minutes} more until the chicken and potatoes are tender, topping up with water to keep them just covered.

Season with more fish sauce, palm sugar and tamarind. Off the heat, stir in the tomatoes and let them soften a few minutes.

Top with @?fried shallots{2%tbsp} or @?crispy garlic{2%tbsp} and serve with @jasmine rice{}.

> The oil may not separate with some coconut milk; carry on regardless.
